[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960087942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107368#issuecomment-2960087942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107368","id":2960087942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wb1uG","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-10T17:32:39Z","updated_at":"2025-06-10T17:32:39Z","body":"Fixes are pushed!\r\n\r\nAs I think about it a bit more, for the description of `enable_fuzzy_matching`:\r\n```\r\nIf [code]true[/code], together with exact matches from the beginning of a filename, the dialog includes approximate matches..\r\n```\r\nIt may be better to swap the order around again, or just omit the \"exact matches from the beginning of a filename\" portion entirely. The focus for this description should be on the fuzzy matching behavior, so frontloading the description of the non-fuzzy behavior instead may be confusing or make it take a bit longer for readers to reach the info they're interested in.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960087942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960115342","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107368#issuecomment-2960115342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107368","id":2960115342,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wb8aO","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-10T17:41:36Z","updated_at":"2025-06-10T17:41:36Z","body":"> The focus for this description should be on the fuzzy matching behavior, so frontloading the description of the non-fuzzy behavior instead may be confusing or make it take a bit longer for readers to reach the info they're interested in.\r\n\r\nI suppose I agree with that. Right now, I am not familiar with fuzzy matching enough to say what _exactly_ needs to be said.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960115342/reac